# PT6: the inverse of the kernel of `⌊|a − b| / 2⌋` over `ZMod 389`

Source: `review/flat_spectrum.md`, *What a part of the table determines*, PT6. The inverse of
`[256 ^ ⌊|a − b| / 2⌋]` mod 389 is symmetric and keeps its form under `x ↦ 96 − x`, so 2401 of its
entries give all of them. They are stored in 9 bits each, row `i` holding `j = i, …, 96 − i`. The
list is only a hint: `E6BlindDet` multiplies it out in the kernel.
-/

